VanForge Database Migrations
===========================

Alembic manages changes to the PostgreSQL database structure.
Run all commands below from the project root.

Configuration
-------------
Database URL: DATABASE_URL in the root .env file
Connection setup: backend/app/database.py
Alembic environment: alembic/env.py
Table definitions: backend/app/models.py
Migration scripts: alembic/versions/

API DTOs in backend/app/dtos/ do not define database tables.

Initialize or update the database
--------------------------------
python -m alembic upgrade head

Run this before starting the backend.
The backend seeds missing professions when it starts.

Create a migration
------------------
1. Apply existing migrations:
   python -m alembic upgrade head

2. Edit the table definitions in backend/app/models.py.

3. Generate a migration:
   python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

4. Review the generated upgrade() and downgrade() functions.

5. Apply the migration:
   python -m alembic upgrade head

Autogenerate compares the SQLModel metadata with the database selected by
DATABASE_URL. Always review its output before applying it.

Check migration status
----------------------
python -m alembic current
python -m alembic history

Version control
---------------
Commit migration scripts alongside the related model changes.
Never commit .env files or database credentials.
